    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into September 2nd with a high-ceiling core anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (73.26), both of whom benefit from favorable matchups against mediocre arms. **Gunnar Henderson** is the clear priority start today; he faces Sugano in a hitter-friendly environment, and with an elite SP skill adjustment (+19%), he is primed for a multi-hit performance. **Luis Robert Jr.** also benefits from this matchup despite a platoon dip, maintaining a strong 69.94 score that cements his status in the lineup. Conversely, while **Kyle Tucker** (50.24) and **Heliot Ramos** (48.17) remain playable, they are facing tough pitchers with sub-3.50 xERAs, dampening their outlook despite their inherent talent. **Sam Antonacci** (62.98) remains a high-value play as he occupies the leadoff spot against Wesneski, leveraging his high-floor approach to maximize scoring potential in a critical Roto stretch.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Wade Meckler** (37.29) and **Liam Hicks** (36.92), both of whom were excluded primarily to protect our game cap usage, as they failed to clear the 40.0 floor. **Wade Meckler** in particular was the \"closest call,\" narrowly edged out because his matchup against Schlittler presents a significant challenge from a pitcher skill perspective (-19%), making the risk of a sub-optimal outcome too great compared to our high-scoring starters. Looking ahead, we continue to monitor **Jacob Wilson** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, who remain sidelined, forcing us to lean on the depth of players like **Miguel Vargas** and **Nasim Nunez**. We are currently navigating these matchups with caution, specifically noting the high SP_xERA for opposing starters like Williamson; should that trend continue, we may see an uptick in late-game production from our middle-order bats like **Coby Mayo**.",
